very poor clinical tone.

Some examples:



SCP-5913 is a humanoid entity dressed up in a bartender suit of the 1920s
附加记录：    

It should be more specific. What is a bartender suit of the 1920s? What does that look like?



subject is measuring
附加记录：    

Grammar issue here. Should be 



the subject shows very little muscle mass, arms are grossly out of proportion with the rest of the body, the subject has shown to have no signs of hair,
附加记录：    

should refer to the SCP rather than 'subject'. This isn't a test log.



I have always observed the subject to have chief strength
附加记录：    

Why are we speaking in first person? SCP files should be written always in third person.



The tendrils that SCP-5913 sprouts out from its body
附加记录：    

Should be  The phrasing suggests that 5913 is consciously sprouting tendrils?





